{"id": "reg-24", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You write regulatory-change digests for the compliance team at Cypress Harbor Credit Union\n(fictional). Read the notice and answer the question in a few words.\n\n# FICTIONAL NOTICE FOR EVALUATION ONLY (not a real rulemaking)\n\nAGENCY: Financial Crimes Enforcement Network (fictional notice).\nACTION: Proposed rule; request for comment.\nSUMMARY: FinCEN proposes to amend 31 CFR part 1020 to lower the recordkeeping threshold for funds transfers from\n$3,000 to $250 for transfers that begin or end outside the United States, and to require institutions to keep those\nrecords for 5 years.\nDATES: Comments must be received on or before February 26, 2027.\n\nSUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION:\n\nSection-by-section analysis, comment 1: Several commenters to the advance notice addressed error-resolution timing. The Bureau considered whether the proposal should apply to institutions of every size and preliminarily concludes that the notice requirement in proposed section 1020.28 should apply uniformly, while seeking comment on alternatives for institutions with fewer than 50 employees and on the cost of compliance for each alternative.\n\nSection-by-section analysis, comment 2: Several commenters to the advance notice addressed payment network rules. The Bureau considered whether the proposal should apply to institutions of every size and preliminarily concludes that the notice requirement in proposed section 1020.19 should apply uniformly, while seeking comment on alternatives for institutions with fewer than 50 employees and on the cost of compliance for each alternative.\n\nSection-by-section analysis, comment 3: Several commenters to the advance notice addressed consumer notice content. The Bureau considered whether the proposal should apply to institutions of every size and preliminarily concludes that the notice requirement in proposed section 1020.28 should apply uniformly, while seeking comment on alternatives for